Let source be "11".
Let target be "1".
Let last source be the last position of source.
Let last target be the last position of target.
Let position be last source.
Let mark be last target.
Let carry be 0.
Let reversed result be empty text.
Repeat while position is at least 0 or mark is at least 0 or carry is 1.
Let sum be carry.
Let digit be 0.
If position is at least 0, set digit to character position of source minus 48.
If position is at least 0, add digit to sum.
If position is at least 0, set position to one less than position.
If mark is at least 0, set digit to character mark of target minus 48.
If mark is at least 0, add digit to sum.
If mark is at least 0, set mark to one less than mark.
Let bit be 48 plus sum modulo 2.
Append bit to reversed result.
Set carry to sum divided by 2.

Let result be empty text.
Let reversed last be the last position of reversed result.
For every step from 0 to reversed last, let number be reversed last minus step, append character number of reversed result to result.
Print result.
